import{H as e,at as t,it as n,vt as r}from"./chunks/framework.dmHZ7NHG.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Command authentication","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"params":{"slug":"command","address":"63d9bf7b-5f2a-8dda-8980-c68ecad8d93e","receipt":"b87bc766-df8b-8d9d-8e2d-99f68e2cb2bd"},"relativePath":"docs/publications/command.md","filePath":"docs/publications/[slug].md"}`),a={name:`docs/publications/command.md`};function o(e,i,a,o,s,c){return r(),n(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="command-authentication" tabindex="-1">Command authentication <a class="header-anchor" href="#command-authentication" aria-label="Permalink to “Command authentication”">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>the auth gate as decidable logic — a command is accepted iff it is signed AND its tag verifies (accept = signed·verifies): unsigned rejected, a failing/tampered tag rejected, exactly one tag verifies, tampering changes the tag, and a LINEAR tag is forgeable (why the real MAC is HMAC-SHA256, KAT-verified, not this model) — the gate logic proven, the strength demarcated</p></blockquote><p>These 7 facts hold by decision. Each was proven in Lean 4 — no Mathlib, checked sorry-free — and every sentence below links the proof that seals it. This note claims nothing beyond what its theorems settle: not that the domain is complete, only that the prose says nothing the proofs do not. It was written by reading the sealed ledger; read the proofs, not the prose.</p><h2 id="the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" tabindex="-1">The facts, each backed by its proof <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" aria-label="Permalink to “The facts, each backed by its proof”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The authentication gate as a truth table: accept(signed, verifies) = signed·verifies over {0,1}² is 1 only when BOTH hold — a command is accepted exactly when it is signed and its tag verifies. — <a href="/theorem/accept_truth_table">proof</a>.</li><li>An unsigned command is never accepted: with no tag (signed = 0), accept(0, v) = 0 whatever the verify bit — no signature, no entry. — <a href="/theorem/unsigned_rejected">proof</a>.</li><li>A failing or tampered tag is rejected: when the tag does not verify (verifies = 0), accept(s, 0) = 0 even if the command is signed — a wrong or altered signature does not pass. — <a href="/theorem/bad_signature_rejected">proof</a>.</li><li>The gate equals its intent: accept(signed, verifies) = (signed ∧ verifies) at every state — the multiplication IS the boolean AND, proven. — <a href="/theorem/accept_matches_spec">proof</a>.</li><li>Exactly ONE presented tag verifies — the correct one (here the expected value 5). Of all 8 candidate tags, only the matching MAC passes; every forgery or tampered tag fails. The gate is precise. — <a href="/theorem/only_correct_tag_verifies">proof</a>.</li><li>Tampering the message changes the tag: for an injective keyed tag mac(k,m) = (7 + m) mod 9, distinct messages carry distinct tags — so an altered message no longer matches the old signature. (A model of the property; the real MAC is HMAC-SHA256.) — <a href="/theorem/tamper_changes_tag">proof</a>.</li><li>Why the MAC must be HMAC-SHA256, not arithmetic: a LINEAR tag t = k ⊕ m is forgeable — (k⊕m₁) ⊕ (m₁⊕m₂) = k⊕m₂, so seeing one command&#39;s tag lets an attacker forge another. Authentication demands a NONLINEAR keyed MAC (HMAC-SHA256, KAT-verified); this is the honest reason the toy tag is refused. — <a href="/theorem/linear_tag_is_forgeable">proof</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="provenance" tabindex="-1">Provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#provenance" aria-label="Permalink to “Provenance”">​</a></h2><p>These 7 proofs fold, order-invariant, to the receipt <code>b87bc766-df8b-8d9d-8e2d-99f68e2cb2bd</code> — recompute it from the same ledger and it returns. The note itself content-addresses to a uuid, so any edit is visible. Writing descends from reading: this note holds only what the proofs it links already sealed, and it was audited by uuidna&#39;s own honesty gate before it was published — a sentence that overreached a proof would have been refused, not shipped.</p><p>Source · <a href="https://github.com/uuidna/uuidna/blob/main/lean/Command.lean" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lean/Command.lean</a> · <a href="/theorems">all theorems</a></p><hr><p><strong>Audited before published</strong> · this note passed uuidna&#39;s honesty gate at build time — every claim above links the proof that seals it. Content-address <code>63d9bf7b</code> · proofs fold to receipt <code>b87bc766</code> (the handles; the full uuids are in this page&#39;s meta, recomputable) · 7 sealed theorems.</p><p><a href="/publications">All publications</a> · <a href="/theorems">All theorems</a> · <a href="/trials">How auditing works</a></p>`,11)]])}var s=e(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};